==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|billy-pot}}

===Etymology===
Scottish, from 19th century. The Australian usage is sometimes claimed to be related to {{m|en|billabong}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 billypot.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Scottish}} A cooking pot.
#* {{circa|1882-1898}}, [[w:Francis James Child|Francis James Child]], ''[[s:Child's Ballads/12|Child's Collected Ballads]]'', 12: [[w:Lord Randall|Lord Randall]],
#*: “What did she boil it in, Willie doo, Willie doo?”
#*: “She boild it in the '''billy-pot'''; die shall I now!”
# {{lb|en|Australia}} A [[billycan]] used to boil tea.

